  "body": "https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/commit-snapshots/cd3bcaeea40b4b9355ae7be3a5799813faa492fc/#interface-nodeiterator\r\n\r\nConsider the scenario at https://jsbin.com/zugoyutice/edit?html,console,output , in particular the removeChild() call. (Derived from https://github.com/tmpvar/jsdom/blob/3743b423cb45657401eef3475a07fd99e015b2e2/test/to-port-to-wpts/node-iterator.js#L429 , for the record)\r\n\r\ntoBeRemovedNode = referenceNode = root = the span\r\n\r\n1. toBeRemovedNode is an inclusive ancestor of referenceNode, so step 1 passes\r\n2. pointerBeforeReferenceNode = true (since it starts that way)\r\n   1. next = null; there is nothing that is not an inclusive descendant of toBeRemovedNode but is an inclusive descendant of root\r\n   2. Do nothing\r\n   3. **Set pointerBeforeReferenceNode to false**\r\n3. **Set referenceNode to the body**\r\n\r\nHowever the test shows that pointerBeforeReferenceNode and referenceNode do not change.\r\n\r\nThis appears to have regressed in https://github.com/whatwg/dom/commit/259775f14d55b21de16cbb0a3c625741fd54aa0b, as jsdom has an implementation based on the older removing-steps-based algorithm, and updating broke <del>a bunch</del><ins>one, after I fixed other bugs of ours :)</ins> of our (to-be-upstreamed) tests.",
